# 🖥️ Operating System Lab Programs (C Language)

## 📌 Overview
This repository contains all **Operating System Lab experiments** implemented in **C language**.  
It includes programs based on CPU Scheduling, Memory Management, File Organization, Disk Scheduling, Page Replacement, and Deadlock concepts.

---

## 📚 Experiments Included

### 🔹 CPU Scheduling Algorithms
- First Come First Serve (FCFS)
- Shortest Job First (SJF)
- Priority Scheduling
- Round Robin Scheduling

---

### 🔹 Page Replacement Algorithms
- FIFO (First In First Out)
- LRU (Least Recently Used)
- Optimal Page Replacement

---

### 🔹 Memory Management Techniques
- MFT (Memory Fixed Partitioning)
- MVT (Memory Variable Partitioning)
- First Fit
- Best Fit
- Worst Fit

---

### 🔹 File Organization Techniques
- Single Level Directory
- Two Level Directory
- Sequential File Allocation
- Indexed File Allocation
- Linked File Allocation

---

### 🔹 Disk Scheduling Algorithms
- FCFS (First Come First Serve)
- SCAN (Elevator Algorithm)
- C-SCAN (Circular SCAN)

---

### 🔹 Deadlock Handling
- Banker’s Algorithm
- Deadlock Prevention Techniques

---

### 🔹 Synchronization Problems
- Dining Philosopher Problem
- Producer-Consumer Problem

---

## ⚙️ Technologies Used
- C Programming Language
- vs code

